  "title": "The Table With Three Corners",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "cooperation",
  "premise": "Three makers want to set a long paper table, but each keeps pulling the sheet toward their own seat and tearing one edge. They add a fourth empty place for the shared food, center the sheet around it, and finally sit without tugging.",
  "hook": "The table is losing this argument.",
  "visible_action": "Paper slides in three directions, stretches into a triangle, then settles as a fourth place setting anchors the composition.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A shared reference can align competing needs.",
  "gate": "The place setting is a storytelling anchor, not a literal guarantee of physical stability.",
